# Line endings are normalised to LF, in the repository and in the working tree.
#
# This is not a style preference. Two things here break under CRLF:
#
#   - `.claude/` fixtures are checksummed in `.claude/.aiae-fixtures-manifest`.
#     CRLF changes the sha256, and `install-managed-claude-fixtures.py` then
#     aborts with "managed fixture was edited locally; refusing overwrite" —
#     a message that misdescribes the cause, since git rewrote the files, not
#     a person. That would block `install-claude-fixtures.sh` permanently.
#
#   - `scripts/*.sh` fail on Linux with "bad interpreter" when they carry CRLF.
#     The AIAE harness adds 22 runtime scripts and 28 checkers to that directory.
#
# `core.autocrlf` is true on at least one machine working on this repository,
# so without this file the next checkout — a branch switch, a `git revert`, a
# fresh clone — silently converts both sets and breaks them.

* text=auto eol=lf
